WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.700
For a few years now, the TV show American
Pickers has been running around the United

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.280
States digging up little pieces of history,
learning fun stories, then spinning them into

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.280
cash.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.960
But who are these representatives of the picking
arts, and what were they like before they

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.740
started carting cameras everywhere?

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.800
Mike Wolfe

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:24.720
Lead picker Mike Wolfe was born on June 11,
1964 in Bettendorf, Iowa, not far away from

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.080
LeClaire, where he'd someday start his flagship
business.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.369
He was picking almost straight out of diapers,
having repaired and flipped a bicycle he found

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.800
lying around his neighborhood at the age of
six for five dollars—a princely sum for

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.000
a little kid.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.059
Not only that, it was the catalyst to his
dream job, so much so that he has worked on

00:00:42.059 --> 00:00:46.050
a book specifically aimed to teach the art
of picking to kids.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:49.410
Also ingrained in him from childhood was a
long-running interest in bikes.

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:54.680
In the '90s, he owned two biking stores and
competed in races, and his ventures into professional

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.030
picking started with quests for old bikes.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:01.590
However, the allure of picking grew too strong
for Mike and he felt the road calling, so

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.870
he bought a van and really got into it.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:07.900
A few road trips later, somebody suggested
to Wolfe that he should take along a video

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.500
camera, and his friend Frank Fritz started
joining in as well.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.680
The pair made a lot of home movies and pitches
over four years before the History Channel

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.380
bit the bait and greenlighted the show.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.380
Frank Fritz

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:23.790
Next, we shift the spotlight to Mike Wolfe's
childhood friend since middle school, Frank

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:24.790
Fritz.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:28.829
He was born on October 11, 1965 in Davenport,
Iowa.

00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:32.860
Most of his life was spent helping others
learn to be safe, as Fritz worked as a fire

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.390
safety inspector for a quarter century, which
led to his first bits of dabbling in picking

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.350
by finding antiques related to firefighting.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:45.329
Like his friend Wolfe, Fritz also has a passion
for motorcycles, having bought his first Harley-Davidson

00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:46.430
as a teenager.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:51.170
These days, he frequently attends the famed
Sturgis motorcycle rally, and at one point

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:56.020
was president of the Davenport American Bikers
Aimed Toward Education chapter, and even gave

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.079
motorcycle safety lessons as well.

00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:02.670
He finally got into the picking business full
time when he opened the shop Frank Fritz Finds

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.470
in 2002, which is still in Savannah, Illinois.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:10.020
He and Wolfe kept crossing paths, and eventually
both men started tagging together professionally

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:14.540
and filming their exploits, leading into the
American Pickers show.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.060
Danielle Colby Cushman

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.690
A constant presence minding the store in LeClaire
while Wolfe and Fritz are out exploring their

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.290
next big item, with the occasional picking
trip thrown in the mix here and there, Danielle

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:29.000
Colby Cushman is also a formidable presence
on the show.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.980
Born on December 3, 1975, Colby was raised
in a family of Jehovah's Witnesses, but her

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:37.170
interests became a lot more varied outside
of the group.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.800
She's also an accomplished burlesque dancer,
to the point that she's toured around the

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.310
country under the name Dannie Diesel (a name
she's had since childhood), founded her own

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:50.220
troupe, Burlesque Le Moustache, and opened
her own dance school in Chicago, Dannie Diesel's

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.760
Bump n' Grind Academy.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.340
She's also a former roller derby girl, a hobby
that spanned three years until injuries put

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.100
an end to it.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.450
Lauren Wray Grisham

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:03.910
One of the managers of the Pickers' Nashville
outpost, Lauren Wray Graham also got into

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.740
the picking business early, through her explorations
of old abandoned farmhouses in her hometown

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:13.820
of Athens, Alabama, working a pawn shop with
her dad, and touring antique stores with her

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:14.820
mom.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.990
When it came time to get her college education,
Grisham moved to Tennessee, out near Nashville.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:22.921
Before she fell in with the Pickers, Grisham
had been serving a stint with Manuel, the

00:03:22.921 --> 00:03:28.070
famed rhinestone-loving costume designer who's
made clothing for rock stars, country legends,

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:30.200
Presidents, and even Salvador Dali.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.770
However, she decided she wanted a "big, new
project," and the Pickers just happened to

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:39.670
be expanding their Antique Archaeology business
into Nashville, setting up shop inside a former

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:40.930
car factory.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:45.340
She joined the team in 2011, and has been
the top representative of the Pickers' southern

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.290
branch ever since.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.290
Robbie Wolfe

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:52.700
Mike's brother Robbie Wolfe is occasionally
seen on the show working to help the Pickers,

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:57.450
especially fulfilling since he shares an interest
with Mike in old vehicles, though Robbie prefers

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.090
automobiles to motorcycles.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:03.060
However, when he's not out with his brother
and the rest of the Pickers crew, Robbie is

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:07.470
back in Davenport, where he's been running
his landscaping company RJ Wolfe and Sons,

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.720
which he founded in the '90s and is still
running to this day.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.110
They offer an impressively varied list of
services including pool installation, putting

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:20.950
in decks, paving driveways new and old, hooking
up lighting, creating "outdoor living spaces,"

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:21.950
and more.

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:25.700
If you're near Iowa and you like Pickers,
Robbie Wolfe can fix up your yard and buy

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.970
some junk from you.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:27.970
Win win.

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:28.970
Thanks for watching!

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:31.880
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.370
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
